\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces  Quantile loss objective \( l \DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow f_\tau (l; T) \) under asymmetric Laplace noise with skewness parameters \( z \in \{-0.9, -0.5, 0, 0.5, 0.9\} \), derived from the limiting form \( x \DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow \exp \left ( -\frac  {|x|}{b}(1 - \mathrm  {sgn}(x) z) \right ) \). Rows correspond to sample sizes \( T \in \{2, 3, 10, 20, 21\} \), and columns correspond to quantile levels \( \tau \in \{0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 0.95\} \). The vertical dashed line marks the true peak location \( L = 22 \). Colors indicate the value of \( z \). }}{15}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
